Adobe Experience Manager (AEM) – Resource Resolver

1. What is Resource Resolver?

"ResourceResolver" is an interface in Adobe Experience Manager (AEM) used to access and retrieve resources from the JCR repository.

It acts as a bridge between the application and repository resources.

2. Why do we use Resource Resolver?

- To retrieve resources from the JCR repository.
- To access content using resource paths.
- To read and modify repository content with appropriate permissions.
- To access resource properties.
- To adapt resources into other useful objects.

3. ResourceResolverFactory

"ResourceResolverFactory" is used to create a ResourceResolver.

It provides different methods to obtain a ResourceResolver.

Important methods

Method| Description
"getResource()"| Retrieves a resource
"getUserID()"| Returns the user ID
"getResourceType()"| Gets the resource type
"getChildren()"| Retrieves child resources
"listChildren()"| Lists child resources
"close()"| Closes the resolver

4. Types of Resource Resolver

1. Request Resource Resolver: Obtained from the current Sling request.
2. Service Resource Resolver: Used for backend operations with configured service-user permissions.
3. Administrative Resource Resolver: Deprecated and should not be used.

5. Real-Time Example

Consider a Campus Food Ordering System.

Suppose menu details are stored in the AEM repository:

/content/food/menu

Using ResourceResolver, we can retrieve the menu resource and access its properties.

6. Java Implementation

@Reference
private ResourceResolverFactory resolverFactory;

public void getMenu() throws LoginException {

    Map<String, Object> params = new HashMap<>();

    params.put(
        ResourceResolverFactory.SUBSERVICE,
        "food-service"
    );

    try (ResourceResolver resolver =
        resolverFactory.getServiceResourceResolver(params)) {

        Resource resource =
            resolver.getResource("/content/food/menu");

        if (resource != null) {
            ValueMap properties = resource.getValueMap();

            String title =
                properties.get("jcr:title", String.class);
        }
    }
}

7. ResourceResolver vs Resource

ResourceResolver| Resource
Provides access to resources| Represents an individual resource
Retrieves resources| Reads resource properties
Can access multiple resources| Represents a particular resource

